* Low-side reverse-polarity NMOS M3 = AOS AO3416 (spice.source: fit), fitted to the datasheet
* AO3416 Rev 5.1 (Dec 2023), p.2 electrical characteristics, see notes/datasheets/ao3416.md.
* AOS publishes no SPICE model on the product page checked (aosmd.com), so these are level-1 fits written for this project.
* Level 1, W = L = 1 (instance size 1), channel plus series resistance: RDS = RS + RD + 1/(KP (VGS - VTO)).
* Datasheet points (25 C, small VDS), typ / max:   VGS 4.5 V: 16 / 22 mOhm,  2.5 V: 18 / 26 mOhm,  1.8 V: 21 / 34 mOhm.
*   NMOS_LOWVGS      typ fit  VTO 0.95, KP 182, RD + RS 14.45 mOhm -> 15.97 / 17.9 / 20.9 mOhm at 4.5 / 2.5 / 1.8 V
*   NMOS_LOWVGS_MAX  max fit  VTO 1.22, KP 119, RD + RS 19.4 mOhm  -> 22.0 / 26.0 / 34.0 mOhm (use for the worst case)
* VTO is an effective value for the fit; the datasheet VGS(th) is 0.4 / 0.7 / 1.1 V (min/typ/max, ID 250 uA). Level 1 has no
* sub-threshold current, so below about 1 V the channel is off and the body diode carries the current (conservative).
* RDS rises about +45 % from 25 C to 125 C (datasheet fig. 4): scale RD/RS in the derating case, not modelled here.
* Capacitance (VGS 0, VDS 10 V, 1 MHz): Ciss 1295 pF typ (1650 max), Coss 160 pF, Crss 87 pF: CGSO = 1.2 nF/m, CGDO = 0.1 nF/m.
* Body diode (source to drain): VSD 0.62 V typ at IS 1 A (IS = 4e-11), Is max 2 A continuous (datasheet).
.model NMOS_LOWVGS NMOS(LEVEL=1 VTO=0.95 KP=182 LAMBDA=0.01 RD=0.007225 RS=0.007225 IS=4e-11 CGSO=1.2e-9 CGDO=1e-10)
.model NMOS_LOWVGS_MAX NMOS(LEVEL=1 VTO=1.22 KP=119 LAMBDA=0.01 RD=0.0097 RS=0.0097 IS=4e-11 CGSO=1.2e-9 CGDO=1e-10)
